//! The reference compute cases of `ps5shader/tests/ref_*.rs` compiled to
//! SPIR-V: each case is decoded, planned, materialised from its user data
//! and result buffer (as the descriptor tables are read from it), laid
//! out, emitted and checked with `spirv-val` when it is installed. The
//! interpreter runs these cases for their results; this checks that the
//! back-end accepts every one of them.
//!
//! The case lists below are generated from the vector files (every
//! `pub const` case in file order).

use super::*;
use ps5shader::resources::{apply_specialization, materialize, BindingLayout, ResourceRuntimeInputs, ShaderResourcePlan};
